          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On December 17, 2012, at 11:30 PM, a witness suddenly saw the sky light up with a deep blue color for 3 seconds from their home. This testimony is very brief; the witness only saw a powerful indirect glow. The color and duration of the phenomenon are consistent with a bolide (atmospheric entry of a meteoroid, or meteorite) that is likely related to the particularly notable Geminid meteor shower this year (see http://clubregulus.free.fr/geminides.html). One could also think of an electrical flash (electric welding, major short circuit on an electrical line) however, the witness does not report the usual flickering of electrical lightning but a complete illumination of the sky (which was overcast), which is well suited to a high-altitude phenomenon. This case is classified as \"B\": probable observation of a bolide.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "2d67a2d8bb2333deeafcba456bd4fede195ead6a86ee9bb0db7734919abf4ea9"
        }
